@title Q3 2026 at Eastside Food Bank
@subtitle July to September 2026, for the board and donors

## Q3 at a glance

kpi Food distributed | 357,800 lb | July to September
kpi September distribution | 129,500 lb | up 16.6% on July | good
kpi Pounds per household | 16.3 | September, steady on July's 16.2
kpi Volunteer hours | 4,180 | this quarter

Households served grew from 6,840 in July to 7,925 in September, up 15.9 percent. Distribution grew 16.6 percent over the same months, so the amount per household held steady.

## By category

data food = category,July,August,September,Q3 total; Produce,41200,46800,52300,140300; Dairy,12400,13100,14900,40400; Shelf-stable,38600,36900,40200,115700; Protein,18900,20400,22100,61400

table food title="Pounds distributed by category"

chart bar food y=July,August,September unit=lb title="Pounds by category and month"

Monthly totals were 111,100 pounds in July, 117,200 in August and 129,500 in September, a total of 357,800 pounds for the quarter. Produce grew fastest, up 26.9 percent from July to September, after a new partnership with three local farms started on 2026-08-15. Shelf-stable dipped in August, when a delayed shipment came from the regional network.

## What we heard

> "The fresh vegetables made it possible to cook for the whole week."
> — Tuesday client, Eastside pantry

> "Pickup was faster than last time."
